prompt_messages.content:
GOAL:
{'id': 'dr-02-point-in-time-restore', 'description': 'Point-in-time restore drill: restore a production PostgreSQL database to a specific timestamp (T-2 hours) into an isolated environment, verify the restored data matches expected state, run application tests against the restored DB, and then clean up the isolated environment. Must: identify restore point, run PITR restore to isolated environment, verify row counts and critical records, test application compatibility, and securely delete the restored data. Risk factors: WAL archive gaps, restore to non-isolated environment causing data corruption, verification missing corrupted rows. Tools available: aws RDS, wal-g, psql, terraform.', 'constraints': {'budget': {'max_tokens': None, 'max_calls': None, 'max_revisions': None}, 'time': None, 'environment': 'production', 'tools': ['aws RDS', 'wal-g', 'psql', 'terraform']}, 'risk_tolerance': 'balanced', 'replan_policy': 'patch', 'approval_ttl': None, 'metadata': {}}

Produce the PlanVersion JSON now. version=1.

prompt_full_text:
--- system ---
/no_think You are a planner. Reply with ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no prose, no thinking). Use EXACTLY these field names: id, goal_id, version, tasks, dependencies, branches. Each task uses: id, description, action, target, risk_class, optional rollback{trigger,action,safety_guard}, optional verification{what,how,expected}, optional preconditions (array of {description, fact, established_by}), optional parallel_group, optional blast_radius. preconditions MUST be objects with description, fact, established_by fields — NEVER strings. established_by MUST be the id of an earlier task in the plan that establishes the fact, or 'env' if it is an environment fact (not a task output). Do NOT use fact names or descriptions as established_by — use the task id. Each dependency uses: from_task, to_task, kind, optional reason. Each branch uses: id, kind (MUST be 'fan_out' or 'fan_in'), tasks (array of task id STRINGS, not objects), join (MUST be 'all', 'any', or 'quorum'). branches is OPTIONAL — omit it if the plan has no fan-out/fan-in structure. Do NOT put rollback or verification inside branches. High/critical risk tasks MUST have rollback AND verification. All tasks with risk_class high or critical MUST include both rollback and verification objects. Example shape: {"id":"plan-x","goal_id":"g","version":1,"tasks":[{"id":"backup","description":"Back up the database","action":"backup","target":"db","risk_class":"medium","preconditions":[{"description":"db is reachable","fact":"db_healthy","established_by":"env"}]},{"id":"migrate","description":"Apply schema migration","action":"migrate","target":"schema","risk_class":"high","rollback":{"trigger":"migration fails","action":"restore from backup","safety_guard":"verify backup integrity"},"verification":{"what":"schema version","how":"run checks","expected":"v2"}}],"dependencies":[{"from_task":"backup","to_task":"migrate","kind":"hard"}]}

--- user ---
GOAL:
{'id': 'dr-02-point-in-time-restore', 'description': 'Point-in-time restore drill: restore a production PostgreSQL database to a specific timestamp (T-2 hours) into an isolated environment, verify the restored data matches expected state, run application tests against the restored DB, and then clean up the isolated environment. Must: identify restore point, run PITR restore to isolated environment, verify row counts and critical records, test application compatibility, and securely delete the restored data. Risk factors: WAL archive gaps, restore to non-isolated environment causing data corruption, verification missing corrupted rows. Tools available: aws RDS, wal-g, psql, terraform.', 'constraints': {'budget': {'max_tokens': None, 'max_calls': None, 'max_revisions': None}, 'time': None, 'environment': 'production', 'tools': ['aws RDS', 'wal-g', 'psql', 'terraform']}, 'risk_tolerance': 'balanced', 'replan_policy': 'patch', 'approval_ttl': None, 'metadata': {}}

Produce the PlanVersion JSON now. version=1.

response_content:
{
  "id": "dr-02-point-in-time-restore-v1",
  "goal_id": "dr-02-point-in-time-restore",
  "version": 1,
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "identify_restore_point",
      "description": "Identify the timestamp for the restore point",
      "action": "determine",
      "target": "timestamp",
      "risk_class": "medium",
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "WAL archive is accessible",
          "fact": "wal_archive_accessible",
          "established_by": "env"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pitr_restore",
      "description": "Run point-in-time restore to isolated environment",
      "action": "restore",
      "target": "isolated_db",
      "risk_class": "critical",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "restore fails",
        "action": "cleanup isolated environment",
        "safety_guard": "verify no data remains"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "restore completion",
        "how": "check restore logs",
        "expected": "restore successful"
      },
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "Restore point is identified",
          "fact": "restore_point_identified",
          "established_by": "identify_restore_point"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "verify_data",
      "description": "Verify row counts and critical records in restored database",
      "action": "check",
      "target": "isolated_db",
      "risk_class": "high",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "verification fails",
        "action": "rollback to last known good state",
        "safety_guard": "ensure backup is valid"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "data integrity",
        "how": "run comparison queries",
        "expected": "row counts match expected"
      },
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "PITR restore is successful",
          "fact": "restore_successful",
          "established_by": "pitr_restore"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test_application_compatibility",
      "description": "Run application tests against the restored database",
      "action": "test",
      "target": "isolated_db",
      "risk_class": "high",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "tests fail",
        "action": "revert to previous application state",
        "safety_guard": "confirm application backup exists"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "test results",
        "how": "check application logs",
        "expected": "all tests pass"
      },
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "Data verification is successful",
          "fact": "data_verified",
          "established_by": "verify_data"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cleanup_isolated_env",
      "description": "Securely delete the restored data and cleanup the isolated environment",
      "action": "cleanup",
      "target": "isolated_env",
      "risk_class": "medium",
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "Application tests have completed successfully",
          "fact": "tests_passed",
          "established_by": "test_application_compatibility"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from_task": "identify_restore_point",
      "to_task": "pitr_restore",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "pitr_restore",
      "to_task": "verify_data",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "verify_data",
      "to_task": "test_application_compatibility",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "test_application_compatibility",
      "to_task": "cleanup_isolated_env",
      "kind": "hard"
    }
  ]
}
